  {
    "insertText": {
      "objectId": "h5d7e580f29331fdc_0_257",
      "insertionIndex": 0,
      "text": "Plain-language explanation of D_side: D is Poisson deviance, summed over the scored sideband bins. It compares the GP's predicted count in each bin with a saturated fit that gives each bin its observed count exactly. Every contribution is nonnegative and vanishes when data equal prediction. For small deviations it approaches (n-b)^2/b. For example, a prediction of100 and an observation of110 contribute approximately0.968. D_side is the sum, and D_side/N_side is the average per scored bin. It is not a p-value or a signal significance. These scored bins lie in50–250MeV outside the local±2.25sigma exclusion. GP uncertainty does not appear as an extra variance term in D; instead the toy comparison repeats the fitted-mean procedure. Because fitting uses these same bins, compare with the refitted-toy band rather than imposing a chi-square/dof expectation of1.\\n\\n"
    }
  }
]
